==English==
{{wikipedia|Sacred cow}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-sacred cow.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} Something which cannot be tampered with, or criticized, for fear of public outcry. A person, institution, belief system, etc. which, for no reason other than the demands of established social etiquette or popular opinion, should be accorded respect or reverence, and not touched, handled or examined too closely.
#* {{quote-journal|en|passage=Many '''sacred cows''' were milked dry in an unbelievable series of outrageous events.|title=That Was The Year That Weren't|work=Cavalier|year=1965|month=December|author=Phil Ochs}}
#* '''1967''', [[w:Paul Krassner|Paul Krassner]], [http://www.ep.tc/realist/74/ ''The Realist, issue 74''], May 1967, front page tagline:
#*: Irreverence is our only '''sacred cow'''.
<!-- Unclear what this citation means:
#* '''1990''', [[w:Reshad Feild|Reshad Feild]], [http://books.google.com/books?id=c7cXAQAAIAAJ ''East west journal, Volume 20''], p.94:
#*: Many people say that I am able to turn '''sacred cows''' into hamburgers.
-->
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2022 January 12|author=Sir Michael Holden|title=Reform of the workforce or death by a thousand cuts?|journal=RAIL|issue=948|page=24|text=In my opinion, in order to save serious amounts of money, a number of ''''sacred cows'''{{'}} will need slaying.}}

